cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KernAdapt, cite this software and record the commit used in your experiments."
type: software
title: "KernAdapt: Adaptive Linux Resource Control for Mixed Workloads"
authors:
  - name: "OSKernel"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lss-lmj/kernadapt-industry-2026"
url: "https://github.com/Lss-lmj/kernadapt-industry-2026"
abstract: >-
  KernAdapt connects workload dependencies and service objectives to Linux
  resource decisions. Its control plane manages configuration selection,
  execution, and recovery, with LockCoop and FlowCausal sched_ext mechanisms
  for lock coordination and tool-workflow scheduling.
keywords:
  - Linux
  - sched_ext
  - eBPF
  - CPU scheduling
  - resource management
  - mixed workloads
  - lock contention
  - workflow scheduling
